::GEO_U06_L04_Q01::
Question ID: GEO_U06_L04_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CGM.15
Question:
Which measurement does surface area represent?
{
~A. The space inside a solid#That is volume.
=B. The total area covering the outside of a solid#Surface area measures the exterior faces or curved surfaces.
~C. The distance around one face#That is perimeter of a face.
~D. The height of the solid#Height is one linear dimension.
}
::GEO_U06_L04_Q02::
Question ID: GEO_U06_L04_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CGM.15
Question:
A cube has side length 4. What is its surface area?
{
~A. 16 square units#This is the area of one face.
~B. 64 cubic units#That is volume.
~C. 24 units#This adds edge lengths, not face areas.
=D. 96 square units#A cube has 6 faces, each 4?=16, so 6(16)=96.
}
::GEO_U06_L04_Q03::
Question ID: GEO_U06_L04_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CGM.15
Question:
Which part of 2pir? + 2pirh represents the two bases of a cylinder?
{
=A. 2pir?#Each base has area pir?, so two bases are 2pir?.
~B. 2pirh#This represents the curved side area.
~C. pirh#This is not the two-base term.
~D. pir?h#This is volume, not base area.
}
::GEO_U06_L04_Q04::
Question ID: GEO_U06_L04_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CGM.15
Question:
Which unit is appropriate for surface area of a cone?
{
~A. cm#Centimeters are linear units.
~B. cm³#Cubic centimeters measure volume.
=C. cm²#Surface area is measured in square units.
~D. degrees#Degrees measure angles.
}
::GEO_U06_L04_Q05::
Question ID: GEO_U06_L04_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CGM.15
Question:
A prism net is made of rectangles. How can the net help find surface area?
{
~A. Multiply all edge lengths#Multiplying all edge lengths does not find surface area.
=B. Find the area of each face and add the areas#A net shows every outside face of the solid.
~C. Find only the largest rectangle#Surface area includes all faces, not only one.
~D. Count the vertices#Vertices do not determine surface area.
}
